.TH RETROSAVER-SETTINGS 1 "2026-10-21" "retrosaver 0.7.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
retrosaver\-settings \- settings window for retrosaver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B retrosaver\-settings
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B retrosaver\-settings
is a GTK 4 and libadwaita window for
.BR retrosaver (1),
which brings classic XScreenSaver display modules back to GNOME on Wayland. It appears in
the GNOME app grid as
.BR Retrosaver .
.PP
The
.B General
page turns the screensaver on or off, which runs
.B retrosaver setup
or
.BR "retrosaver teardown" ,
and sets how long the session must be idle before the screensaver starts, how often it
switches modules, and when the session locks and the display turns off. Times are shown
in minutes. A delay that is not a whole number of minutes is shown rounded, labelled with
its exact value, and left alone unless it is changed.
.PP
The
.B Modules
page lists every installed display module with its description, to tick the ones the
screensaver may show. In
.B "All modules except unticked ones"
mode the unticked modules are written to
.BR EXCLUDE ;
in
.B "Only ticked modules"
mode the ticked ones are written to
.BR INCLUDE .
.PP
Each module's play button shows it in a window of its own, through
.BR "retrosaver preview" .
Pressing it again, or another module's, stops it, as does closing either window. While a
preview is open the app holds an idle inhibitor, so the screensaver does not start and
the session does not lock over it.
.PP
Changes are saved half a second after the last one, with no Apply button, and a running
daemon picks them up by itself.
.SH NOTES
The window never reads or writes the configuration file directly. It runs
.BR "retrosaver config show \-\-json" ,
.BR "retrosaver config set" ,
.B "retrosaver list \-\-all \-\-json"
and
.BR "retrosaver preview" ,
so the file is parsed and validated in one place. A file that does not parse is reported
and nothing is edited until it is fixed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RETROSAVER
The
.B retrosaver
executable to run, instead of the one on
.BR PATH ;
for running from a source tree.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Passed on to
.BR retrosaver ,
which reads its configuration from
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/retrosaver/retrosaver.conf .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/retrosaver/retrosaver.conf
The configuration the window edits, through
.BR retrosaver .
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/us.prem.Retrosaver.desktop
The desktop entry that puts
.B Retrosaver
in the app grid.
.TP
.I /usr/share/metainfo/us.prem.Retrosaver.metainfo.xml
The AppStream description that software centres such as GNOME Software show.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR retrosaver (1)
.PP
